<div class="h-100 overflow-auto p-2 p-md-3">
    <div class="alert alert-info d-flex gap-3 align-items-start" role="status">
        <i class="bi bi-door-open fs-3" aria-hidden="true"></i>
        <div>
            <h2 class="h5 alert-heading mb-1">Sorry to see you go</h2>
            <p class="mb-0">
                If you are moving to another software provider, Customer Exit gives you a documented copy of your
                Trade Control business data and tenant-owned files.
            </p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <h2 class="h5">About this export</h2>
    <p>
        This facility supports the HMRC production-credentials requirement that customers can obtain their data
        when changing software provider. It does not imply HMRC endorsement or certification of Trade Control.
    </p>

    <div class="row g-3 mb-3">
        <div class="col-12 col-lg-6">
            <section class="border rounded h-100 p-3" aria-labelledby="customer-exit-includes">
                <h3 id="customer-exit-includes" class="h6">
                    <i class="bi bi-file-earmark-zip me-2" aria-hidden="true"></i>What the archive contains
                </h3>
                <ul class="mb-0">
                    <li>A manifest explaining the archive structure and exclusions.</li>
                    <li>Supported physical business tables as documented UTF-8 JSON.</li>
                    <li>Your tenant-owned documents, images and templates in their original formats.</li>
                    <li>A unique export reference and SHA-256 integrity digest.</li>
                </ul>
            </section>
        </div>
        <div class="col-12 col-lg-6">
            <section class="border rounded h-100 p-3" aria-labelledby="customer-exit-excludes">
                <h3 id="customer-exit-excludes" class="h6">
                    <i class="bi bi-shield-lock me-2" aria-hidden="true"></i>What the archive excludes
                </h3>
                <ul class="mb-0">
                    <li>Passwords, cryptographic private keys and infrastructure configuration.</li>
                    <li>OAuth grants, access or refresh tokens and vendor credentials.</li>
                    <li>Operational event logs and information belonging to another tenant.</li>
                    <li>Automatic migration into another product.</li>
                </ul>
            </section>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="alert alert-warning" role="note" id="customer-exit-warning">
        <strong>Keep the download secure.</strong> It contains sensitive business and personal data. Store it in an
        access-controlled location and transfer it only to a provider you trust. Generating the archive is recorded
        in your tenant Event Viewer.
    </div>

    <p>
        Downloading an archive does <strong>not</strong> close your account, cancel your service, delete any data or
        authorise a tax filing. Those actions are separate and require their own instructions.
    </p>

    <form method="get" action="/Admin/CustomerExit/Download" class="border rounded p-3 bg-light">
        <div class="form-check mb-3">
            <input class="form-check-input"
                   type="checkbox"
                   id="confirmCustomerExit"
                   name="confirmed"
                   value="true"
                   @bind="_confirmed"
                   aria-describedby="customer-exit-warning" />
            <label class="form-check-label" for="confirmCustomerExit">
                I understand what this archive contains and want to generate it now.
            </label>
        </div>

        <button type="submit"
                class="btn btn-primary"
                disabled="@(!_confirmed)">
            <i class="bi bi-download me-2" aria-hidden="true"></i>Generate and download archive
        </button>
    </form>

    <p class="small text-muted mt-3 mb-0">
        <a href="https://tradecontrol.github.io/admin/admin-manager-customer-exit"
           target="_blank"
           rel="noopener noreferrer">Read the Customer Exit guide</a>
        for archive contents, security precautions and next steps.
    </p>
</div>

@code {
    private bool _confirmed;
}
